.SS "template<typename Var, uint32_t dim> void \fBcsmp::DataInputVisitor\fP< Var, dim >::Visit (\fBFace\fP< dim > * f)\fR [virtual]\fP"
The key method of the visitor design pattern\&. Visit() must be defined for the target object (for instance \fBNode\fP objects, or \fBElement\fP objects)\&. Since the argument is the actual object, its entire interface is accessible to the visitor in order to carry out operations\&. Overload this method in the derived class to gain access to target objects and perform the actions that are desired for the visitation\&. 
